 r←Test_TableEdit_035(stopFlag batchFlag);parms;n;⎕TRAP;table;rowTitles;msg
⍝ Test "lock" of columns. The first two columns should not participate in horizontal scolling.
 r←T._Inactive
 :Return

 r←T._Failed
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 :If batchFlag
     r←¯1
 :Else
     table←⍪'Obama' 'Bush' 'Clinton' 'Reagan' 'Kennedy'
     table,←'Barak' 'George' 'Bill' 'Ronald' 'John'
     table,←?5 200⍴1000000
     parms←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Table.CreateParms
     parms.posn←35 25
     parms.size←400 600
     parms.caption←'Test_Table_004: locking columns'
     parms.confirmQuit←0
     parms.testMode←1
     parms.lock←2

     msg←'In this test you shall scroll horizontally. The first two columns should stay put. When you are ready to continue press <Enter>'
     CommTools.Pause msg

     n←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Table.Create table #.APLGUI.APLGUI.APLGuiGlobalParms.CreateDefaults parms

     r←~1 CommTools.YesOrNo'Are the first two columns excluded from horizontal scrolling?'

∆TidyUp:
     n.∆CloseForm
 :EndIf
